186505080 #edb/ref 1074 "Sometimes, it's handy to assign a number to each equation in a system, so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\{7x - 7y - 35 = 0(1); 2x - 4y - 6 = 0(2)\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{blue}(2)$, we can solve for $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 2x - 4y - 6 &= 0 \\\\ 2x - 4y &= 6 \\\\ 2x &= 6 + 4y \\\\ x &= \\dfrac{6 + 4y}{2} \\\\ x &= 3 + 2y \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=3+2y$ into equation $\\color{red}(1)$ and solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 7x - 7y - 35 &= 0 \\\\ 7(3 + 2y) - 7y - 35 &= 0 \\\\ 21 + 14y - 7y - 35 &= 0 \\\\ -14 + 7y &= 0 \\\\ 7y &= 14 \\\\ y &= 2 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute\n\n$$\ny=2\n$$\n\ninto equation $\\color{red}(1)$, then we can find the value of $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 7x - 7y - 35 &= 0 \\\\ 7x - 7\\left(2\\right) - 35 &= 0 \\\\ 7x - 14 - 35 &= 0 \\\\ 7x - 49 &= 0 \\\\ 7x &= 49 \\\\ x &= 7 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=7$ and\n\n$$\ny=2\n$$\n\n, which can be written as\n\n$$\n\\left(7,2\\right)\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186505081 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186505035 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186505081 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186505081 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$\\{4b + 32 = 0; 5a + 2b - 19 = 0$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186505081 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e7e74981-78de-5721-8c70-6b15d18904de" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186505081 #edb/ref 1074 "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{red}(1)$, we can solve for $b$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 4b + 32 &= 0 \\\\ 4b &= -32 \\\\ b &= -8 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=-8$ into equation $\\color{blue}(2)$ and solve for $a$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 5a + 2b - 19 &= 0 \\\\ 5a + 2\\left(-8\\right) - 19 &= 0 \\\\ 5a - 16 - 19 &= 0 \\\\ 5a &= 35 \\\\ a &= 7 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a - b = 7 - \\left(-8\\right) = 15$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186505084 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186505056 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186505084 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186505084 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$\\{-10x - 10y + 7 = 0; 4x + 8y - 16 = 0$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186505084 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ed97dc9b-b6f4-5076-b3bb-6acac17b72a7" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186505084 #edb/ref 1074 "Sometimes, it's handy to assign a number to each equation in a system, so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\{-10x - 10y + 7 = 0(1); 4x + 8y - 16 = 0(2)\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{blue}(2)$, we can solve for $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 4x + 8y - 16 &= 0 \\\\ 4x + 8y &= 16 \\\\ 4x &= 16 - 8y \\\\ x &= \\dfrac{16 - 8y}{4} \\\\ x &= 4 - 2y \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=4-2y$ into equation $\\color{red}(1)$ and solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -10x - 10y + 7 &= 0 \\\\ -10(4 - 2y) - 10y + 7 &= 0 \\\\ -40 + 20y - 10y + 7 &= 0 \\\\ -33 + 10y &= 0 \\\\ 10y &= 33 \\\\ y &= \\dfrac{33}{10} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{33}{10}\n$$\n\ninto equation $\\color{red}(1)$, then we can find the value of $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -10x - 10y + 7 &= 0 \\\\ -10x - 10\\left(\\dfrac{33}{10}\\right) + 7 &= 0 \\\\ -10x - 33 + 7 &= 0 \\\\ -10x - 26 &= 0 \\\\ -10x &= 26 \\\\ x &= -\\dfrac{13}{5} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-\\dfrac{13}{5}$ and\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{33}{10}\n$$\n\n, which can be written as\n\n$$\n\\left(-\\dfrac{13}{5},\\dfrac{33}{10}\\right)\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186505092 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186073753.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186505092 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "9ae46e73-14e1-5b95-998d-0a81f435ef96" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508171 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508208 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508171 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508171 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$\\{3a-3b=-18; -2a+b=7$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508171 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "01d4210c-99cb-5509-8003-8615f9f2d644" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508171 #edb/ref 1074 "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2a+b & =7 \\\\ b & =7+2a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=7+2a$ into the first equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a-3b & =-18 \\\\ 3a-3(7+2a) & =-18 \\\\ 3a-21-6a & =-18 \\\\ -3a-21 & =-18 \\\\ -3a & =3 \\\\ a & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-1$ into $b=7+2a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =7+2(-1) \\\\ b & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a-b=-1-(5)=-6.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508174 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508191 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508174 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508225 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508174 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508174 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of equations:\n$\\{x+5y=21; y=x-3$\nFind the solution $(x, y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.The solution is\n$($\n{{field-1}}\n$, $\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508174 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1814dd75-6dc3-5a88-93bf-56fa1a5ec858" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508174 #edb/ref 1074 "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nNotice that the second equation is already solved for $y:$\n\n$$\ny=x-3\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $y$ in the first equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+5y & =21 \\\\ x+5(x-3) & =21 \\\\ x+5x-15 & =21 \\\\ 6x-15 & =21 \\\\ 6x & =36 \\\\ x & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $x=6$ into $y=x-3,$ we can then find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =(6)-3 \\\\ y & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=6,\\,y=3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508179 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508232 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508179 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508179 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$\\{-3a-2b=2; -3a+b=8$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508179 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2e8faafd-e3ef-5205-a5d6-b458af26d97f" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508179 #edb/ref 1074 "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3a+b & =8 \\\\ b & =8+3a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=8+3a$ into the first equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3a-2b & =2 \\\\ -3a-2(8+3a) & =2 \\\\ -3a-16-6a & =2 \\\\ -9a-16 & =2 \\\\ -9a & =18 \\\\ a & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-2$ into $b=8+3a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =8+3(-2) \\\\ b & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a-b=-2-(2)=-4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508187 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508224 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508187 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508240 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508187 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508187 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the solution $(x,y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$\\{3x+3y=2; 3x+y=-5$\n\nThe solution is $($ {{field-1}} $, $ {{field-2}} $)$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508187 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3db3cd07-1246-5ea5-a44f-5fee48dd9a13" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508187 #edb/ref 1074 "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+y & =-5 \\\\ y & =-5-3x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y=-5-3x$ into the first equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+3y & =2 \\\\ 3x+3(-5-3x) & =2 \\\\ 3x-15-9x & =2 \\\\ -6x-15 & =2 \\\\ -6x & =17 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{17}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $x=-\\frac{17}{6}$ into $y=-5-3x,$ we can then find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-5-3(-\\frac{17}{6}) \\\\ y & =\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-\\frac{17}{6},\\,y=\\frac{7}{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508204 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508170 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508204 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508209 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508204 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508204 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the solution $(x,y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$\\{-3x+4y=8; -2x+y=6$\n\nThe solution is $($ {{field-1}} $, $ {{field-2}} $)$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508204 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "76c476e0-406c-5751-a806-f5cbe03fe610" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508204 #edb/ref 1074 "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+y & =6 \\\\ y & =6+2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y=6+2x$ into the first equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x+4y & =8 \\\\ -3x+4(6+2x) & =8 \\\\ -3x+24+8x & =8 \\\\ 5x+24 & =8 \\\\ 5x & =-16 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{16}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $x=-\\frac{16}{5}$ into $y=6+2x,$ we can then find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =6+2(-\\frac{16}{5}) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-\\frac{16}{5},\\,y=-\\frac{2}{5}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508205 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508193 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508205 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508205 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$\\{-5a+2b=9; -3a+b=3$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508205 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7afeeb08-8b8f-54f1-86b4-033f592e20d8" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508205 #edb/ref 1074 "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3a+b & =3 \\\\ b & =3+3a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=3+3a$ into the first equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5a+2b & =9 \\\\ -5a+2(3+3a) & =9 \\\\ -5a+6+6a & =9 \\\\ a+6 & =9 \\\\ a & =3 \\\\ a & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=3$ into $b=3+3a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =3+3(3) \\\\ b & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a-b=3-(12)=-9.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508207 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508178 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508207 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508207 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $p - q$?\n\n$\\{4p=-24; p+5q=19$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508207 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7c5faa09-66e6-54c1-b548-04286527c92b" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508207 #edb/ref 1074 "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the first equation, we can isolate $p$ by dividing both sides by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4p & =-24 \\\\ p & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $p=-6$ into the second equation and solve for $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p+5q & =19 \\\\ (-6)+5q & =19 \\\\ 5q & =25 \\\\ q & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p-q=-6-(5)=-11.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508210 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508231 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508210 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508210 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$\\{-3a-3b=6; -4a+b=-7$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508210 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "873b7f6f-85bd-5d73-adb8-dc5d593e552e" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508210 #edb/ref 1074 "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4a+b & =-7 \\\\ b & =-7+4a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=-7+4a$ into the first equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3a-3b & =6 \\\\ -3a-3(-7+4a) & =6 \\\\ -3a+21-12a & =6 \\\\ -15a+21 & =6 \\\\ -15a & =-15 \\\\ a & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=1$ into $b=-7+4a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =-7+4(1) \\\\ b & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a-b=1-(-3)=4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508214 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508181 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508214 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508216 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508214 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508214 #edb/ref 1071 "The coefficients $a$ and $b$ satisfy $b=135-11a.$\n\nThe coefficients $a$ and $b$ also satisfy the equation $7b+162a=435.$ Find the values of $a$ and $b.$\n\n$a\\,=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$b\\,=$\n{{field-2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508214 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "92720f95-de85-556b-8f87-1b3810fd832e" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508214 #edb/ref 1074 "We have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}b &=135-11a \\\\ 7b+162a &=435\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nNotice that the first equation is already solved for $b:$\n\n$$\nb=135-11a\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $b$ in the second equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7b+162a & =435 \\\\ 7(135-11a)+162a & =435 \\\\ 945-77a+162a & =435 \\\\ 945+85a & =435 \\\\ 85a & =-510 \\\\ a & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-6$ into $b=135-11a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =135-11(-6) \\\\ b & =201\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=-6,\\,b=201.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508215 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508218 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508215 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508215 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$\\{-2a-4b=-14; -2a+b=6$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508215 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9362a51f-6c19-5264-931e-57aaf13ce3e6" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508215 #edb/ref 1074 "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2a+b & =6 \\\\ b & =6+2a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=6+2a$ into the first equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2a-4b & =-14 \\\\ -2a-4(6+2a) & =-14 \\\\ -2a-24-8a & =-14 \\\\ -10a-24 & =-14 \\\\ -10a & =10 \\\\ a & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-1$ into $b=6+2a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =6+2(-1) \\\\ b & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a-b=-1-(4)=-5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508227 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508192 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508227 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508228 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508227 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508227 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the solution $(x,y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$\\{5x-2y=5; 2x+y=-1$\n\nThe solution is $($ {{field-1}} $, $ {{field-2}} $)$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508227 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b0966484-f411-5cf8-8677-c24b7843a43c" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508227 #edb/ref 1074 "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+y & =-1 \\\\ y & =-1-2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y=-1-2x$ into the first equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-2y & =5 \\\\ 5x-2(-1-2x) & =5 \\\\ 5x+2+4x & =5 \\\\ 9x+2 & =5 \\\\ 9x & =3 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $x=\\frac{1}{3}$ into $y=-1-2x,$ we can then find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-1-2(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=\\frac{1}{3},\\,y=-\\frac{5}{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508233 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508182 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508233 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508190 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508233 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508233 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the solution $(x,y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$\\{2x+2y=12; -2x+y=5$\n\nThe solution is $($ {{field-1}} $, $ {{field-2}} $)$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508233 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ddedcc45-5aba-5229-89b3-d8e7abbe4344" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508233 #edb/ref 1074 "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+y & =5 \\\\ y & =5+2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y=5+2x$ into the first equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+2y & =12 \\\\ 2x+2(5+2x) & =12 \\\\ 2x+10+4x & =12 \\\\ 6x+10 & =12 \\\\ 6x & =2 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $x=\\frac{1}{3}$ into $y=5+2x,$ we can then find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =5+2(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\ y & =\\frac{17}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=\\frac{1}{3},\\,y=\\frac{17}{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508241 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186073752.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186508241 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "f056eadd-a598-5e78-b365-4bdfdf9e1094" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186544085 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186544957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544085 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186544989 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544085 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186544995 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544085 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544085 #edb/ref 1045 "Introduction to Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544085 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186544957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544085 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544085 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048652 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544085 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "f68627be-ff54-526c-8208-8406616b4322" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544118 #edb/ref 1080 "19" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544118 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544118 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0f66ec8e-8bae-5a96-a179-d8e3a1dfe2cc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544168 #edb/ref 1080 "6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544168 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544168 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2522a912-6ec9-5d1e-9006-2d6a985f8f29" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544197 #edb/ref 1080 "8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544197 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544197 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3182f7a3-fd37-55